{"resource":{"id":"operating-systems-common-mistakes","title":"Operating Systems — Common Mistakes","category":"CS Core","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"13 min","pages":17,"lastUpdated":"October 2026","tags":["OS","Systems","CS Core"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"OS troubleshooting handbook: scheduling mistakes, synchronization bugs, deadlocks, race conditions, paging errors, segmentation faults, virtual memory issues, Linux permissions, and filesystem errors."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"intro","label":"Introduction"},{"id":"concepts","label":"Core Concepts"},{"id":"steps","label":"Step-by-Step Explanations"},{"id":"diagrams","label":"Process & Memory Diagrams"},{"id":"scheduling","label":"Scheduling Charts & Tables"},{"id":"examples","label":"Real-world Examples"},{"id":"applications","label":"Practical Applications"},{"id":"practices","label":"Best Practices"},{"id":"mistakes","label":"Common Mistakes"},{"id":"tips","label":"Tips & Tricks"},{"id":"compare","label":"Comparison Table"},{"id":"commands","label":"Linux Command Reference"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary & Key Takeaways"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQs"},{"id":"references","label":"Further Reading & References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Operating Systems — Complete Tutorial","tag":"CS Core","time":"75 min"},{"title":"Operating Systems — Cheat Sheet","tag":"CS Core","time":"6 min"},{"title":"Operating Systems — Interview Questions","tag":"CS Core","time":"44 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Master the concepts presented in Operating Systems — Common Mistakes.</li>\n          <li>Understand how processes, threads, scheduling, and memory management work in modern OSes.</li>\n          <li>Apply filesystem, synchronization, and virtualization ideas to real Linux systems.</li>\n          <li>Recognize best practices, common mistakes, and productive tips.</li>\n          <li>Prepare confidently for exams, interviews, and hands-on systems work.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"intro\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Introduction</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>OS troubleshooting handbook: scheduling mistakes, synchronization bugs, deadlocks, race conditions, paging errors, segmentation faults, virtual memory issues, Linux permissions, and filesystem errors.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-sky-500/40 bg-sky-500/10 text-sky-900 dark:text-sky-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"M12 16v-4\"/><path d=\"M12 8h.01\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Who this is for</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Students, engineers, and interview candidates preparing to build strong operating systems fundamentals.</div></div></div></div>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1629654297299-c8506221ca97?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Operating Systems overview: kernel, user space, processes, and the layers between hardware and applications.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"concepts\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Core Concepts</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>An operating system is the software layer that manages hardware and provides services to user programs. Its core responsibilities are process management, memory management, storage/filesystems, device I/O, and protection.</p>\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><b>Kernel vs user mode</b> — the CPU enforces a privilege boundary so untrusted code cannot touch hardware directly.</li>\n          <li><b>Processes & threads</b> — processes isolate memory; threads share memory and are the unit of scheduling.</li>\n          <li><b>Scheduling</b> — the kernel decides which runnable thread gets the CPU next.</li>\n          <li><b>Virtual memory</b> — every process sees its own address space, mapped to physical frames on demand.</li>\n          <li><b>Filesystems</b> — persistent, hierarchical storage on top of block devices.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"steps\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Step-by-Step Explanations</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>User invokes a program; the shell calls <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>fork()</code></pre></div> then <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>execve()</code></pre></div>.</li>\n          <li>Kernel creates a task_struct, allocates a virtual address space, and loads the ELF binary.</li>\n          <li>Scheduler places the new task on a runqueue; a context switch lets it run.</li>\n          <li>Page faults populate physical frames on demand; the MMU translates addresses.</li>\n          <li>System calls (<div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>read</code></pre></div>, <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>write</code></pre></div>, <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>mmap</code></pre></div>) cross into kernel mode to touch hardware.</li>\n          <li>On <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>exit()</code></pre></div> the kernel reclaims memory, closes descriptors, and notifies the parent.</li>\n        </ol>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"diagrams\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Process &amp; Memory Diagrams</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1629654857987-a0d09ce2a5cf?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Process lifecycle and virtual memory layout: text, data, heap, stack, and kernel space.\" />\n        <pre class=\"overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border/60 bg-muted/40 p-4 text-xs leading-relaxed\">\nProcess states:\n   new  ─►  ready  ─►  running  ─►  terminated\n                ▲          │\n                └── waiting ◄── I/O / event\n\nVirtual address space (Linux x86_64):\n   ┌────────────── kernel space ──────────────┐\n   │                                          │\n   ├────────────── stack ▼ ───────────────────┤\n   │           (mmap region)                  │\n   ├────────────── heap ▲ ────────────────────┤\n   ├────────────── bss / data ────────────────┤\n   └────────────── text (code) ───────────────┘\n        </pre>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"scheduling\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Scheduling Charts &amp; Tables</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n          <table class=\"w-full text-sm\">\n            <thead>\n              <tr class=\"border-b border-border/60 text-left\">\n                <th class=\"py-2 pr-4\">Algorithm</th>\n                <th class=\"py-2 pr-4\">Preemptive</th>\n                <th class=\"py-2 pr-4\">Avg Wait</th>\n                <th class=\"py-2\">Best For</th>\n              </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody class=\"[&>tr]:border-b [&>tr]:border-border/40\">\n              <tr><td class=\"py-2 pr-4\">FCFS</td><td>No</td><td>High</td><td>Batch jobs</td></tr>\n              <tr><td class=\"py-2 pr-4\">SJF</td><td>Optional</td><td>Lowest (theoretical)</td><td>Known burst times</td></tr>\n              <tr><td class=\"py-2 pr-4\">Round Robin</td><td>Yes</td><td>Fair</td><td>Interactive systems</td></tr>\n              <tr><td class=\"py-2 pr-4\">Priority</td><td>Yes / No</td><td>Depends</td><td>Real-time & mixed loads</td></tr>\n              <tr><td class=\"py-2 pr-4\">MLFQ</td><td>Yes</td><td>Adaptive</td><td>General-purpose OSes</td></tr>\n              <tr><td class=\"py-2 pr-4\">CFS (Linux)</td><td>Yes</td><td>Fair (vruntime)</td><td>Modern Linux desktops/servers</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"examples\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Real-world Examples</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><b>Linux</b> — CFS scheduler, ext4/xfs/btrfs filesystems, cgroups powering containers.</li>\n          <li><b>Windows NT</b> — hybrid kernel, NTFS, and priority-based scheduling with boosts.</li>\n          <li><b>macOS / iOS</b> — XNU hybrid kernel with Mach + BSD layers.</li>\n          <li><b>Android</b> — Linux kernel plus binder IPC and Zygote process model.</li>\n          <li><b>Real-time OS</b> — FreeRTOS/VxWorks with deterministic scheduling for embedded systems.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"applications\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Practical Applications</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>OS knowledge underpins backend engineering (performance, concurrency), DevOps (containers, Linux administration), embedded/IoT, cloud infrastructure, security engineering, and low-level performance tuning.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"practices\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Best Practices</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Prefer immutable / append-only data structures where possible to reduce locking.</li>\n          <li>Use OS primitives (mutex, semaphore, condvar) instead of hand-rolled spinlocks.</li>\n          <li>Cap open file descriptors and threads; monitor with <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>ulimit</code></pre></div>, <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>lsof</code></pre></div>, <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>top</code></pre></div>.</li>\n          <li>Keep filesystems tuned: right block size, journaling mode, and mount options.</li>\n          <li>Profile before optimizing — <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>perf</code></pre></div>, <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>strace</code></pre></div>, <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>bpftrace</code></pre></div> beat guesses.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"mistakes\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Common Mistakes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Assuming <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>fork()</code></pre></div> copies memory eagerly — it uses copy-on-write.</li>\n          <li>Ignoring signal handling and leaving zombies with unreaped children.</li>\n          <li>Sharing mutable data between threads without synchronization.</li>\n          <li>Confusing paging with segmentation, or virtual with physical memory.</li>\n          <li>Running production services as root without capabilities/namespaces.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"tips\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Tips &amp; Tricks</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>htop</code></pre></div> and <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>btop</code></pre></div> give a live picture of CPU, memory, and threads.</li>\n          <li><div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>strace -f -p PID</code></pre></div> shows every syscall a running process makes.</li>\n          <li><div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>/proc/&amp;lt;pid&amp;gt;/</code></pre></div> exposes maps, fds, status — priceless for debugging.</li>\n          <li>Use <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>nice</code></pre></div>/<div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>ionice</code></pre></div> for background jobs so they don't starve interactive work.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"compare\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Comparison Table</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n          <table class=\"w-full text-sm\">\n            <thead>\n              <tr class=\"border-b border-border/60 text-left\">\n                <th class=\"py-2 pr-4\">Aspect</th>\n                <th class=\"py-2 pr-4\">Process</th>\n                <th class=\"py-2 pr-4\">Thread</th>\n                <th class=\"py-2\">Container</th>\n              </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody class=\"[&>tr]:border-b [&>tr]:border-border/40\">\n              <tr><td class=\"py-2 pr-4\">Isolation</td><td>Strong (own address space)</td><td>None (shared)</td><td>Namespaces + cgroups</td></tr>\n              <tr><td class=\"py-2 pr-4\">Creation cost</td><td>Higher</td><td>Low</td><td>Low (shared kernel)</td></tr>\n              <tr><td class=\"py-2 pr-4\">Fault blast radius</td><td>Contained</td><td>Whole process</td><td>Contained</td></tr>\n              <tr><td class=\"py-2 pr-4\">Typical use</td><td>Separate services</td><td>Parallel work in-service</td><td>Deployable app units</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"commands\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Linux Command Reference</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>code</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code># Processes\nps aux | grep nginx\ntop / htop\nkill -9 &lt;pid&gt;\n\n# Memory\nfree -h\nvmstat 1\ncat /proc/meminfo\n\n# Filesystems\ndf -h\ndu -sh *\nmount | column -t\n\n# Scheduling / priority\nnice -n 10 ./job\nrenice -n -5 -p &lt;pid&gt;\n\n# Tracing\nstrace -f ./app\nperf top</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Operating systems mediate between hardware and applications.</li>\n          <li>Processes isolate; threads share; both are scheduled by the kernel.</li>\n          <li>Virtual memory, filesystems, and syscalls are the universal abstractions.</li>\n          <li>Modern OS trends: containers, unikernels, eBPF, and specialized schedulers.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Do I need to learn assembly to understand OS?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">No — a high-level grasp of C-level memory models is enough for most engineering roles.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Is Linux the best OS to learn on?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Yes — it is open source, ubiquitous in industry, and every concept has readable code behind it.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>How much math is involved?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Very little beyond simple arithmetic for scheduling and memory calculations.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Should I read the Linux kernel source?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Skim it after you understand the concepts — start with schedulers and VFS.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Further Reading &amp; References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><a class=\"text-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://www.os-book.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Operating System Concepts — Silberschatz, Galvin, Gagne</a></li>\n          <li><a class=\"text-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://cs.vu.nl/~ast/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Modern Operating Systems — Tanenbaum</a></li>\n          <li><a class=\"text-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://man7.org/tlpi/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">The Linux Programming Interface — Michael Kerrisk</a></li>\n          <li><a class=\"text-primary hover:underline\" href=\"https://pages.cs.wisc.edu/~remzi/OSTEP/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">OSTEP — Operating Systems: Three Easy Pieces (free online)</a></li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">This resource is provided for educational purposes only. Commands and configuration examples may differ across distributions and kernel versions — always verify against the official documentation for your environment before applying in production.</p>\n      </div></section>"}